The quickest and surest way to convert is to sacrifice a unicorn of
your (current) alignment on another alignment's altar.

For example, a couple of games ago I wanted to ascend a lawful orcish
barbarian.   So I sacrificed a black unicorn on a lawful altar.
Presto! Lawful barbarian.

There are some side effects.

1) You lose any protection immediately, and have to buy it back.
2) You experience divine anger.  It will take some sacrificing to
mollify that, and if you're converting to chaotic it's even harder.

If I was converting a lawful character to a chaotic alignment, the
simplest thing to do would be to find a chaotic altar and reverse
genocide white unicorns. That gives me my conversion gift, a
reconciliation gift, and throws in a couple of unicorn horns in the
bargain that are all for me.  They polypile into magic markers with
some frequency.

There is *another* method as well... I don't remember for certain, but
I think if you manage to push your alignment down into the deep
negative (consistently healing creatures if you're chaotic, killing
peacefuls if you're lawful), there's a chance an altar sacrifice on a
foreign altar will convert *you* instead of the altar.  But I don't
use that method because 1) It's only a possibility, not a certainty.
2) It's deucedly hard to get your alignment down really low, because
every time you vanquish a cross-aligned monster, alignment goes up a
point. If you're a hack-n-slasher like I am who just can't resist the
urge to fight, it's very difficult to get an alignment below pious.

Oh yes, one other thing you should be aware of ... after you convert
all *existing* creatures of your old alignment will remain peaceful.
However, any new ones will be hostile.  And vice versa.

For example, again let's remember my converted lawful orc.   Any
dwarfs I encountered up to that point were hostile, because I had been
chaotic.  But all dwarfs generated after conversion were peaceful.
Likewise, fellow orcs prior to conversion were and remained peaceful,
but any generated afterwards were hostile.

I have ascended two converted characters of the opposite alignment
they started with (after the quest, natch). I recommend it for
anyone .. it's quite fun.

